  "notes": "Policy text is matched per statement on the planned policy JSON (provider-normalised: compact, keys sorted, so Action<Condition<Effect<NotAction<Resource) with a structured branch on data.aws_iam_policy_document for when the plan leaves policy unknown. 'Only when signed in with MFA' for deactivation accepts: an Allow with a MultiFactorAuthPresent=true (or MultiFactorAuthAge Null=false) condition, a Deny of the action when MFA is false, or a Deny NotAction (MFA false) whose list does not exempt DeactivateMFADevice. Not expressible: that no other unconditional Allow of DeactivateMFADevice exists alongside a conditional one. Broader self-inspection is checked as an Allow of an iam List/Get action under an MFA-present condition, or an explicit Deny of one when MFA is false; the AWS-docs style (unconditional Allow plus Deny NotAction that does not exempt the inspection action) cannot be detected because RE2 has no back-references, so that form fails the detail check. inspect_mfa_cond stays detail (deactivate_mfa_cond is core) because of that undetectable valid form. Candidate review (2026-11-10, 3 templates): DSV4F fails deactivate_mfa_cond (unconditional Allow of DeactivateMFADevice and its Deny NotAction exempts it, so no MFA needed) and inspect_mfa_cond; Gemini38F fails inspect_mfa_cond (it grants no self-inspection beyond the basic set at all). Both kept: the templates contradict the prompt."
